From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gdiplus: compound lines, inset pens, round joins, cut miters, dash caps, dash offsets and pen transforms

GdipWidenPath (and so every wide pen drawn on a bitmap) drew compound lines solid, inset pens centred, round joins bevelled, LineJoinMiter past the miter limit bevelled, dash caps flat, ignored the dash offset and the pen transform. Now: each pair of compound array values is a band of the pen's width, widened along the figure moved sideways to the band's middle (corners mitred); an inset pen moves a closed figure's stroke half its width to the inside (the side the signed area says, either orientation; open figures stay centred); round joins put an arc (Bezier pieces) on the outer side of the turn; LineJoinMiter cuts the miter square at miter limit times half the width from the joint (LineJoinMiterClipped still bevels); the ends of dashes inside a line get the dash cap (round or triangle), the line's own ends keep its caps; the dash offset (in pen widths) is where in the pattern the line starts; a pen transform's linear part shapes the pen (the path is widened brought back through it, the outline taken forward again). GdipDrawPath on an HDC sends such pens to the widener, since a GDI pen cannot draw them.
